# Sample lock file. Phase 1 of redesign generates the real one via pip-compile. DO NOT commit hand-edited locks.
#
# spec_id: 70ab2170-381a-4657-bcd1-28a40c6f369b (v2.1)
# Source:  pipeline_mcp_data/specs/agent-kb-redesign-spec-v2.1.json
#          implementation.phases[1] "Phase 1 — Pattern A single-launcher runtime bootstrap"
#
# This is a SAMPLE lockfile derived from the current pyproject.toml runtime
# dependencies (agent-knowledgebase v0.7.0) with strict version pins. Phase 1
# of the redesign replaces this with a real lock generated by:
#
#     pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements.lock pyproject.toml
#
# Until then, this file documents the dependency surface that bin/run_server.py
# (Phase 1 launcher) will install into ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.venv on first
# launch. The SHA256 of this file is the sentinel checked against
# .venv/.req-sha to determine if pip install should re-run.
#
# After Phase 5 ships, the lock will shrink — sentence-transformers and
# tree-sitter-languages move to optional extras and DROP OUT of the default
# install. The realistic floor will then be ~700MB (chromadb ~400MB +
# tree-sitter-languages stays for codebase ingestor + httpx + pydantic + mcp
# + tiktoken + trafilatura).
#
# DO NOT hand-edit this file. Use `pip-compile` to regenerate.

# --- runtime dependencies (current v0.7.0 surface, awaiting Phase 5 trim) ---

